</span><strong><span style="background: #f0f6ff">Date:</span></strong><span style="background: #f0f6ff">
March 2026<br/>
</span><strong><span style="background: #f0f6ff">Prepared
for:</span></strong><span style="background: #f0f6ff"> Executive Team
&amp; Dev Team<br/>
</span><strong><span style="background: #f0f6ff">Status:</span></strong><span style="background: #f0f6ff">
Pre-launch — pending approvals noted below </span></span>
</p>
<p>This document summarises every change made to the TeamPod landing
page from the original file to its current state. It is intended to
give the executive team full visibility of what was changed and why,
and to flag the items that still require a decision or asset before
the page can go live.</p>
<h2>1. Page Structure — Section Reorder</h2>
<p>The page section order was restructured to follow a SAR
copywriting framework (Situation → Agitate → Resolve).
High-impact content now appears earlier, while the page holds trust
and pricing until after the visitor understands the value.</p>
