	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Headline</p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>&quot;Trusted by UK
			Finance Teams&quot; → &quot;What Finance Teams Say&quot;</p>
		</td>
	</tr>
</table>
<p style="margin-left: 0.17in; margin-right: 0.17in; margin-top: 0.17in; margin-bottom: 0.17in">
<span style="display: inline-block; border-top: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: 3.00pt solid #f59e0b; border-right: none; padding-top: 0in; padding-bottom: 0in; padding-left: 0.17in; padding-right: 0in"><strong><span style="background: #fffbeb">Pending:</span></strong><span style="background: #fffbeb">
Replace initials avatars with real customer photos and obtain written
consent for use of names and quotes before publishing.</span></span></p>
<h2>10. Integrations Section</h2>
<p>Section subtext shortened from 2 sentences to 1. Content
unchanged. Integration logos (QuickBooks, SAGE, Xero SVGs) retained
as-is.</p>
<h2>11. Footer</h2>
<table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="2">
	<tr>
		<th style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Item</p>
		</th>
		<th style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Change</p>
		</th>
		<th style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Reason</p>
		</th>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Resources column</p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Removed entirely</p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Help Centre, User Guide,
			API Docs, Case Studies, and Video Tutorials do not exist. Dead
			links damage trust and SEO.</p>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Social media icons</p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>LinkedIn and Twitter
			removed</p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>No active accounts to
			link to. Only the email icon remains.</p>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Email links</p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>All email addresses
			converted to mailto: links with pre-filled subject (&quot;Webpage
			Questions&quot;) and opening body</p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Reduces friction for
			inbound enquiries</p>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Product links</p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>All now anchor correctly
			to page sections (#features, #pricing, #integrations, #security,
			#faq)</p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Previously all linked to
			#</p>
		</td>
	</tr>
</table>
<p><strong>Note on mailto: links:</strong> These open the user's
default mail app (Outlook, Apple Mail). This is correct behaviour for
a B2B audience who typically have Outlook configured. If a web-based
contact form is preferred, this should be added post-launch — no
action needed before go-live.</p>
