<h2>Pending Decisions — Executive Team</h2>
<p style="margin-left: 0.17in; margin-right: 0.17in; margin-top: 0.17in; margin-bottom: 0.17in">
<span style="display: inline-block; border-top: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: 3.00pt solid #f59e0b; border-right: none; padding-top: 0in; padding-bottom: 0in; padding-left: 0.17in; padding-right: 0in"><strong><span style="background: #fffbeb">These
items must be resolved before the page goes live.</span></strong></span></p>
<table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="2">
	<tr>
		<th style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Item</p>
		</th>
		<th style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Decision Required</p>
		</th>
		<th style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Impact</p>
		</th>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p><strong>Favicon</strong></p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Asset does not exist.
			Needs to be created and supplied.</p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Missing favicon looks
			unprofessional in browser tabs and bookmarks</p>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p><strong>Logo</strong></p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Final approved version
			needs sign-off before go-live.</p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Cannot publish without
			confirmed brand asset</p>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p><strong>£100 Credit vs
			Free Trial</strong></p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Page consistently
			references £100 Free Credit. Confirm this is the live offer. Hero
			CTA, pricing section, and FAQ all reference it.</p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Inconsistency between
			offer types at launch damages trust</p>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p><strong>Pricing model</strong></p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Current per-page volume
			band model requires visitors to calculate their own monthly cost —
			adds friction. Consider a 3-tier flat monthly structure (Starter /
			Growth / Scale) as used by Dext and Hubdoc.</p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Conversion rate risk.
			Recommend resolving before launch if possible.</p>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p><strong>Demo booking</strong></p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>&quot;Book a 15-Min Demo&quot;
			CTA button currently links to #. Needs a Calendly or Microsoft
			Bookings URL. Recommend Calendly (free tier available, Google &amp;
			Outlook compatible).</p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>CTA button non-functional
			at launch</p>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p><strong>Social media</strong></p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>LinkedIn and Twitter
			removed from footer — no active accounts. Confirm whether
			accounts will be created for launch.</p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Absence of social
			presence may affect trust signals</p>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p><strong>Customer quotes</strong></p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Confirm all three
			testimonials are from real customers and that written consent has
			been obtained for use of full names and quotes publicly.</p>
		</td>
		<td style="border: none; padding: 0in"><p>Legal risk if quotes are
			illustrative and not confirmed</p>
		</td>
	</tr>
</table>
